  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Verizon Business Network Services obligated $355M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Verizon Business Network Services won 371 awards so far, with an average award size of $956K. Verizon Business Network Services obligations are down 18.7% year over year. Verizon Business Network Services annual obligations have moved from $265M in FY21 to $496M in FY22, $380M in FY23, $459M in FY24, $436M in FY25, and $355M in FY26. Verizon Business Network Services top buyers in FY2026 to date are the Department of Defense with $115M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $93.6M, followed by the Department of Justice with $55.9M and the Social Security Administration with $29.6M. Verizon Business Network Services principal markets are Wired Telecommunications Carriers with $301M and Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) with $28.8M. Verizon Business Network Services also records activity under Telecommunications Resellers and Other Computer Related Services alongside smaller NAICS categories.",
